    "id": "p36-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Show that in any collection of four natural numbers, at least two will leave the same remainder when divided by 3.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "There are only three possible remainders, $0$, $1$ and $2$. By the pigeonhole principle, at least two of the four numbers have the same remainder.",
      "worked": "Label three holes with the possible remainders $0$, $1$ and $2$ when divided by $3$. Place each of the four numbers into the hole corresponding to its remainder.\n\nBy the pigeonhole principle, four numbers placed into three holes give at least two numbers in one hole. These numbers leave the same remainder when divided by $3$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
